hild health) from AUT University, New Zealand, and a MA in Development Studies (with a focus on Global Health) from the University of Auckland, New Zealand.<br \/><br \/><\/div><div>Tineke&#8217;s research expertise and focus is on social science and participatory research with children\/youth, public health, humanitarian response and disaster\/emergency response (HIV, nutrition, diarrheic disease) and health care ethics. She continues to work with organization&#8217;s\/universities to support research and postgraduate study; and consults for international NGOs related to child\/maternal\/public health; in addition to continuing to publish in international journals.<\/div>\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<section class=\"elementor-section elementor-top-section elementor-element elementor-element-75aa4ea elementor-section-boxed elementor-section-gap-beside-yes elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-height-default elementor-section-column-vertical-align-stretch\" data-id=\"75aa4ea\" data-element_type=\"section\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-container elementor-column-gap-extended\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-column elementor-col-100 elementor-top-column elementor-element elementor-element-04d0975\" data-id=\"04d0975\" data-element_type=\"column\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-wrap elementor-element-populated\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-71c0245 elementor-widget elementor-widget-spacer\" data-id=\"71c0245\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"spacer.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-spacer-inner\"><\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<\/section>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>\u00ab Go back to Our People page Visiting Faculty Dr. Tineke Water\u200b Visiting Professor of Public Health Dr Tineke WATER is a Public Health Consultant with the World Bank Cambodia and Academic Advisor for Future Forum, an independent policy think tank for young researchers,\u00a0 and visiting Professor of Public Health at the Cambodian University of Technology, Phnom Penh, Cambodia. She holds a PhD (child health) from AUT University, New Zealand, and a MA in Development Studies (with a focus on Global Health) from the University of Auckland, New Zealand. Tineke&#8217;s research expertise and focus is on social science and participatory research with children\/youth, public health, humanitarian response and disaster\/emergency response (HIV, nutrition, diarrheic disease) and health care ethics. She continues to work with organization&#8217;s\/universities to support research and postgraduate study; and consults for international NGOs related to child\/maternal\/public health; in addition to continuing to publish in international journals.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":0,"parent":9580,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"elementor_header_footer","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"class_list":["post-16417","page","type-page","status-publish","hentry","post-no-thumbnail"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/16417","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/page"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/4"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=16417"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/pages\/16417\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":33082,"href":"https:\/\/camtech.edu.kh\/